---
import Seo from "../components/Seo.astro";
import AnalyticsConsent from "../components/AnalyticsConsent.astro";
const contact = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_PRIVACY_CONTACT || "";
if (contact && !/^mailto:[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/.test(contact)) throw new Error("PUBLIC_PRIVACY_CONTACT must be a mailto address.");
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <Seo title="Privacy & analytics — mono-agent" description="What the Mono Agent marketing site measures, what it leaves out, and how to control optional analytics." path="/privacy/" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="wrap privacy-page">
      <a href="/">Back to mono-agent</a>
      <h1>Privacy &amp; analytics</h1>
      <p>This notice covers the marketing website, operated by Robert Sreberski—not agents you run yourself or the separate documentation website.</p>
      <h2>You choose whether to share analytics</h2>
      <p>Optional traffic analytics use Vercel Web Analytics. Its collection script is loaded only after you choose “Allow analytics”. “No thanks”, Global Privacy Control and Do Not Track keep analytics off. The site works without analytics or JavaScript.</p>
      <p>Use “Analytics preferences” here or in the landing-page footer to change your choice. Withdrawal stops future collection and normally reloads the page to unload the script; it does not erase data already received. Your choice is stored in local storage for up to 180 days. If storage cannot save a withdrawal, collection stops on this page but the choice may not persist. Permission for our previous analytics provider is not reused.</p>
      <h2>What is measured</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Page views and aggregate visitor counts for this marketing site.</li>
        <li>Referrer information supplied by your browser, approximate location, and device, browser and operating-system categories.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We remove query strings and fragments from measured page URLs. We do not send custom click or copy events, form contents, account identities, session recordings or newsletter data. Vercel uses a request-derived visitor hash that resets daily rather than tracking cookies or our own stored session identifier; it is not a cross-device or cross-site identity. We use the Hobby plan’s one-month reporting window, not a promise that the provider deletes data after one month.</p>
      <p>Vercel receives connection information, including IP address and browser headers, to serve the site and process analytics. This is not an EU-only ingestion configuration. See Vercel’s documentation for its processing and retention policies.</p>
      <button class="analytics-settings" type="button" hidden>Analytics preferences</button>
      <p class="analytics-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
      <h2>Hosting and third-party links</h2>
      <p>Vercel serves this site and may process request/security logs under its own policies. GitHub and the documentation site have their own behavior when you follow a link. This site does not currently offer a newsletter signup.</p>
      <p><a href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-policy">Vercel Web Analytics privacy</a> · <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy">Vercel privacy policy</a></p>
      <p>Site operator: <a href="https://github.com/robertsreberski">Robert Sreberski</a>. Please do not post personal data in public issues.</p>
      {contact && <><h2>Questions and data requests</h2><p>Contact <a href={contact}>the site operator</a> privately about this website’s data processing.</p></>}
      <p>Last updated: 20 September 2026.</p>
    </main>
    <section class="analytics-notice" aria-label="Optional analytics" hidden>
      <p><strong>Help us understand what’s useful.</strong> Allow basic traffic analytics with Vercel? No cookies or session replay. <a href="/privacy/">Details</a></p>
      <div><button type="button" data-consent="no">No thanks</button><button type="button" data-consent="yes">Allow analytics</button></div>
    </section>
    <AnalyticsConsent />
  </body>
</html>
